// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_susp_network_sniffing.yml
// ID Sigma: ba1f7802-adc7-48b4-9ecb-81e227fddfd5
// Título: Potential Network Sniffing Activity Using Network Tools
// Descripción: Detects potential network sniffing via use of network tools such as "tshark", "windump".
Network sniffing refers to using the network interface on a system to monitor or capture information sent over a wired or wireless connection.
An adversary may place a network interface into promiscuous mode to passively access data in transit over the network, or use span ports to capture a larger amount of data.

// Fecha de creación: 2019-10-21
// Fecha de modificación: 2023-02-20
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_susp_network_sniffing.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\tshark.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-i") or FolderPath endswith "\\windump.exe"
